# sweep: --seed-root examples/books/fixtures/formats
# Every kind of file Books lists: Markdown, HTML and text open in the reader,
# a damaged EPUB says it could not be opened, and a PDF goes to the Kobo
# reader shelf and says where it opens. Enough files are seeded that the
# Library shelf turns pages both ways.
wait-for Library
expect 15 books
expect Kobo reader
shot books-many
tap Library
wait-for 1 of
shot books-library-shelf
tap-id next
wait-for 2 of
tap-id previous
wait-for 1 of
# Each book closes back to the shelf it was opened from.
tap-paged A Letter Home
wait-for hill behind the house
shot books-text
tap-id 4294967295
wait-for 1 of
expect-missing hill behind the house
tap-paged Damaged
wait-for could not be opened
expect-missing not a zip
shot books-damaged
tap-id 4294967295
wait-for 1 of
tap-paged Index of Streets
wait-for Market Street runs east
shot books-html
tap-id 4294967295
wait-for of 
tap-paged Notes on a Rainy Afternoon
wait-for kettle boiled
expect-missing # Notes
shot books-markdown
tap-id 4294967295
wait-for of 
tap-id 4294967295
wait-for Your books
# What was opened is on the Recent shelf, newest first, and the last
# readable book is offered to continue.
expect Continue reading
expect Recent
tap Recent
wait-for Notes on a Rainy Afternoon
expect Index of Streets
expect A Letter Home
expect-missing Damaged
shot books-recent
tap-id 4294967295
wait-for Your books
tap Kobo reader
wait-for Timetable
tap Timetable
wait-for PDFs open in the Kobo reader
shot books-pdf
tap-id 4294967295
wait-for Timetable
